* testbench.spice -- `klt pex` testbench body for the cdac_array sub-block
* (issue #1017): the DAC transfer characteristic of sim/cdac-array-transfer's
* own methodology (testbench/tb_cdac_array_transfer.spice, issue #53), re-cast
* around the layout's own extracted subckt interface so `klt pex` can swap the
* single `.include` below for its freshly `--parasitics`-extracted netlist and
* diff the schematic leg against the extracted leg, per corner, per code.
*
* As in the transfer campaign, each of the 5 representative 9-bit
* sub-array codes (0, 128, 256, 384, 511) gets its OWN instance of the array --
* P side driven with the code directly, N side with the 9-bit mirrored
* complement -- reset to Vcm by an ideal testbench-only switch until t=1n while
* every bottom plate sits at its pre-code baseline (SEL high, bit=0 -> VREFN),
* then released: at t=1n every bit-1 position's real bottom-plate switch moves
* its bottom plate to VREFP. The settled top-plate pair at t=500n
* (>> RC of any active path) is that code's DAC output, read via the .meas rows
* of the pex request run_pex.py builds. Ideal expected value computed
* independently in run_pex.py: vdiff_ideal(code) = vdd*(2*code-511)/512.
*
* Pin order on every X line below is the EXTRACTED netlist's own (alphabetical)
* order -- layout/cdac-array/reports/LATEST's cdac_array.extract.spice declares
*   .SUBCKT cdac_array SELn0..SELn8 SELp0..SELp8 TOP_N TOP_P VDD VREFN VREFP VSS
* run_pex.py asserts the current extraction still declares exactly this list
* before running, so a re-draw that reorders pins fails loudly here instead of
* silently permuting nets.
*
* CORNER AXES: `vdd` and `vcm` are literal DC sources keyed by corners.supply_v
* in the request run_pex.py builds (the `alter` gotcha: only a named SOURCE is
* an alter target -- layout/comparator/pex/README.md). VCM tracks the rail
* (VCM = VDD/2) as a PAIRED supply point, never independently swept -- the
* settled top-plate value depends on the reset baseline, so a VCM that did not
* follow its corner's rail would swamp the comparison with a ~(VDD/2 - 0.9 V)
* offset, orders of magnitude above an LSB. VREFP is not a separate source at
* all: DR-003 ratifies V_REF = V_DD at the rail, so every VREFP pin below is
* wired straight to the vdd rail node, as are the bit=0 SEL pins. On both PEX
* legs the pulsed SEL and reset highs are fixed at 1.8 V and SWMOD Vt at 0.9 V.
* The transfer campaign uses VDD and VDD/2 respectively, so those levels
* differ at the 1.62 V and 1.98 V corners.

Vdd    vdd    0 DC 1.8
Vrefn  vrefn  0 DC 0
Vss    vss    0 DC 0
Vcm    vcm    0 DC 0.9

* Shared ideal reset-switch control (testbench-only): closed (high) before t=1n
* pins every top node to Vcm; open after lets charge redistribute.
Vctrl_reset nctrl_reset 0 pwl(0 1.8 0.9n 1.8 1.1n 0 500n 0)
.model SWMOD SW(Ron=1 Roff=1e12 Vt=0.9 Vh=0.05)

.include "cdac_array_pex_reference.spice"

* ---- code=0  (P code=0, N code=511) ----
Vsel_0n0 sel_0n0 0 pwl(0 1.8 0.9n 1.8 1.1n 0 500n 0)
Vsel_0n1 sel_0n1 0 pwl(0 1.8 0.9n 1.8 1.1n 0 500n 0)
Vsel_0n2 sel_0n2 0 pwl(0 1.8 0.9n 1.8 1.1n 0 500n 0)
Vsel_0n3 sel_0n3 0 pwl(0 1.8 0.9n 1.8 1.1n 0 500n 0)
Vsel_0n4 sel_0n4 0 pwl(0 1.8 0.9n 1.8 1.1n 0 500n 0)
Vsel_0n5 sel_0n5 0 pwl(0 1.8 0.9n 1.8 1.1n 0 500n 0)
Vsel_0n6 sel_0n6 0 pwl(0 1.8 0.9n 1.8 1.1n 0 500n 0)
Vsel_0n7 sel_0n7 0 pwl(0 1.8 0.9n 1.8 1.1n 0 500n 0)
Vsel_0n8 sel_0n8 0 pwl(0 1.8 0.9n 1.8 1.1n 0 500n 0)
Xarr_0 sel_0n0 sel_0n1 sel_0n2 sel_0n3 sel_0n4 sel_0n5 sel_0n6 sel_0n7 sel_0n8 vdd vdd vdd vdd vdd vdd vdd vdd vdd top_0n top_0p vdd vrefn vdd vss cdac_array
Sreset_0p top_0p vcm nctrl_reset 0 SWMOD
Rdc_0p top_0p vcm 1T
Sreset_0n top_0n vcm nctrl_reset 0 SWMOD
Rdc_0n top_0n vcm 1T

